  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The length of a rope is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span>. When a force is applied to the rope it extends to a length of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{1}\"></span>. Then the rope is released and it contracts. The work done by the rope as it contracts from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{1}\"></span> to its original length is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span>. Assuming that the force applied is proportional to the length of the rope, what is the energy required to extend the rope to a length of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2x_{1}-x_{0}\"></span>?</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2W\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3W\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4W\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
